This branch (Person 2: graphs, features, and named pattern detection) is original
code written for the RingBreaker hackathon. It does not copy source from
Mule-Hunter-Engine or LedgerZero.

Design references consulted but not copied:

- LedgerZero (Apache License 2.0), https://github.com/Concurrents-org/LedgerZero
  Inspected for payment/user/device field names and graph relationship ideas
  (users, devices, IPs, timestamped payments). No LedgerZero source files were
  included in this tree.

- Mule-Hunter-Engine (no license file present at time of inspection)
  Inspected only as conceptual/algorithmic reference for useful graph statistics
  and ring shapes. No Mule Hunter source was copied. Label-derived features
  (community_fraud_rate, second_hop_fraud_rate) are intentionally not implemented.

Dashboard and engine (October 2026 rebuild): the analyst dashboard
(dashboard/src), including the D3 network graph, and the runtime engine
(ringbreaker/engine) are original code. The earlier LedgerZero-derived
NetworkGraph.tsx has been removed. The dashboard's visual layout took general
inspiration from a design mock-up; no code or assets were copied from it.
